# /etc/default/earlyoom on nous (source: utils/nous/memory-guard/earlyoom).
# Act only when available RAM is at or below 5% (SIGKILL at 3%) and free swap
# at or below 10% (5%): the 32 GiB swapfile absorbs cold agent pages first, and
# earlyoom fires just before the kernel's own OOM path thrashes the host for
# minutes. Kill single processes, preferring browsers and build/test jobs;
# avoid inference, remote access (herdr is the phone's session server) and
# agent sessions unless nothing else is left.
EARLYOOM_ARGS="-m 5,3 -s 10,5 -r 0 --prefer ^(chrome|chrome_crashpad|chromium|headless_shell|pytest|clang|cc1|cc1plus|ld|rustc|node)$ --avoid ^(llama-server|sshd|tailscaled|herdr|systemd|systemd-journal|dbus-daemon|omp)$"
